In human terms: Do whatever the hell you want with these workflows. Sell what they
make, fork them, gut them for parts, we don't care. Just don't blame us when a
graph fills your VRAM and takes the desktop with it. That's a you problem.

The license covers the workflow files. It says nothing about the checkpoints, LoRAs,
or custom nodes a graph loads. Those carry their own terms, and some of them
restrict commercial use. Check before you ship.
